{{also|Folgen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|volgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|folgēn}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*folgēn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fulgāną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfɔlɡŋ̩/|/ˈfɔlɡən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-folgen.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<sein,haben>}}

# {{lb|de|with dative object|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[follow]] (on the same path or in a sequence)
#: {{ux|de|Der Held '''folgte''' dem Drachen zu seinem Höhle.|The hero '''followed''' the dragon to its cave.}}
#: {{ux|de|Drei Jahre später '''folgte''' eine Fortsetzung des ersten Films.|Three years later a sequel '''followed''' the first film.}}
# {{lb|de|with dative object|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[understand]], to be [[attentive]] to
#: {{ux|de|Ich konnte der Handlung des Films nicht '''folgen'''.|I couldn't '''follow''' the plot of the film.}}
# {{lb|de|with {{m|de|aus|tr=from}}|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[follow]] (as a consequence), to [[come of]], to [[result]] from
#: {{ux|de|Daraus '''folgt''', dass der Butler es getan hat.|It '''follows''' that the butler did it.}}
# {{lb|de|with dative object|auxiliary {{m|de|haben}}}} to [[obey]] (rules, the law), to [[follow]] (instructions, advice)
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe entschieden, Ihrem Rat zu '''folgen'''.|I've decided to '''follow''' your advice.}}

